  "dom_id": "step-q12549",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given $P(A)=0.25$, $P(B)=0.75$, $P(A\\cup B)=0.8$, determine whether  $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events.",
  "worked_solution": "To check if $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive, we must check that $P(A\\cap B)=0.$\n\nWe can calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.25+0.75-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.25+0.75-0.8 \\\\  & =0.2\\ne 0.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ and $B$ are not mutually exclusive events.",
